{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["And Moshe brought back the words of the people to YHWH — on the next day, as he proceeds to explain: ״ויאמר ה' אל משה הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן״ and so forth (Exodus 19:9)." "Then — ״ויגד משה את דברי העם אל ה'״ (Exodus 19:8)." "This is — ״וישב משה״ and so forth (Exodus 19:8) — a summary statement. Afterward it specifies: thus Moshe said to the Holy One, blessed be He: they have already, since yesterday, taken upon themselves to do whatever You command them. And similarly: ״ותצא אש מלפני ה' ותאכל את העולה״ (Leviticus 9:24), and in the midst of this — ״ויקחו שני בני אהרן נדב ואביהוא״ and so forth (Leviticus 10:1). ״ותצא אש מלפני ה'״: the fire found Nadav and Avihu in front of the golden altar inside the sanctuary, as they offered alien fire upon it, and burned them; then it went outside and consumed the burnt offering on the bronze altar in the courtyard, outside the sanctuary. And so in the book of Judges, in the section of Micah: ״וישב את אלף ומאה הכסף לאמו ותאמר אמו הקדיש הקדשתי את הכסף לה'״ and so forth (Judges 17:3), ״וישב את הכסף לאמו״ (Judges 17:4). First the verse states: ״וישב את הכסף לאמו״. And afterward it explains how: ״ותאמר אמו״ and so forth, ״וישב הכסף לאמו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "Rashbam cites Leviticus 10:2 as ״ותצא אש מלפני ה'״; the verse reads ותצא rather than ותצא, but the reference is to the fire that consumed Nadav and Avihu. The lengthy interpolation about the fire's path between altars is Rashbam's own peshat reconstruction of the sequence."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:11.077207057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}